# Game 8 — White versus 20k

Result: Black wins by 34 points (B+34), after W58 pass and B59 pass. Chinese area, komi 7, simple ko, no suicide. Captures before scoring: none. Exact record: game-008.sgf. Six scored games, eight losses, no demonstrated win. All seven previous notes were read. Existing-group distinct liberties were listed after every opponent board move; the opening lone Black stone was inspected manually. No engine, Monte Carlo, move-ranking program, or future-sequence search was used. Conclusions are manual and do not establish optimal alternatives.

Opening: W2 C3, W4 C7, then W6 D5 attached to Black E5. B7 D6 left D5 with {C5,D4}; W8 D4 extended to four liberties. W10 E4 and W12 E3 expanded toward the bottom, but B13 F2 and B15 E2 restricted that direction. White switched to D7/E7/F7 above Black's center. B17 E6 joined D6/E5/F6, and B19 C6 separated the upper and lower White frameworks. The lower group's outside liberties remained {C4,C5,D3,F3} before W20 C5, but its usable lower space was already contracting. This was the moment to check actual eye boundaries, not merely the count.

