Right-side connection: W46 H5 began without two secured independent eye regions. B47 H4 removed the direct bottom route; W48 H6 and B49 G5 left H5/H6 with {G6,J5,J6}, while Black G7/H7 had {G6,J7}. White changed the plan to an outside connection instead of continuing down the edge. W50 J7 had {J6,J8}; B51 G6 joined Black's upper and central chains. White's H5/H6 then had {J5,J6}, and J7 had {J6,J8}. W52 J8 joined J7 to the upper White chain, with seven liberties. B53 J5 put H5/H6 in atari at J6. W54 J6 joined the WHOLE upper group to those two stones and left six liberties, all in the upper interior. This checked connection avoided another isolated-group loss. It gained only a few area points; it did not solve the lower group's problem.

